  },
  data: {
    LLM: 'The lead rotates each round; the first round leader is chosen by chance. The player who is offered the lead must set a double; if they have no double, the lead passes left until someone can. Others build a train from one side only of the lead double; the first tile is played crosswise to mark the start. If you have a tile matching the open end you play it; otherwise you pass. The game ends when blocked or when one player dominoes.',
    Player: 'The lead rotates each round; the first round leader is chosen by chance. The player who is offered the lead must set a double; if they have no double, the lead passes left until someone can. Others build a train from one side only of the lead double; the first tile is played crosswise to mark the start. If you have a tile matching the open end you play it; otherwise you pass. The game ends when blocked or when one player dominoes.',
    objective: 'Score points by setting doubles. When you set a double you score one point for it plus one point for each double already in the train that is lower than yours. First player or team to reach 60 points wins the game.',
    gameplay: 'The lead rotates each round; the first round leader is chosen by chance. The player who is offered the lead must set a double; if they have no double, the lead passes left until someone can. Others build a train from one side only of the lead double; the first tile is played crosswise to mark the start. If you have a tile matching the open end you play it; otherwise you pass. The game ends when blocked or when one player dominoes.',
    keyRules: [
      'Double-6 set; four players; seven tiles each; no boneyard',
      'Leader must set a double or pass lead left',
      'Train builds from one side only of the lead double; first tile crosswise',
      'Match open end or pass',
      'Doubles order for scoring: 0-0 through 6-6, then 0-0 again (double blank is both high and low)',
      'Game is 60 points',
    ],
